<img width="350" height="525" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Balsamic-Chicken-Marinade-350x525.jpg" class="webfeedsFeaturedVisual wp-post-image" alt="Balsamic marinated grilled chicken on a plate from the top view." style="display: block; margin-bottom: 5px; clear:both;max-width: 100%;" link_thumbnail="" decoding="async" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Balsamic-Chicken-Marinade-350x525.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Balsamic-Chicken-Marinade-768x1152.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Balsamic-Chicken-Marinade-1024x1536.jpg 1024w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Balsamic-Chicken-Marinade-400x600.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Balsamic-Chicken-Marinade-150x225.jpg 150w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/Balsamic-Chicken-Marinade.jpg 1200w" sizes="(max-width: 350px) 100vw, 350px" />
<div class="wp-block-group is-layout-constrained wp-block-group-is-layout-constrained">
<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Whether you&rsquo;re cooking on the grill, in the oven, or on the stovetop, this versatile marinade transforms everyday chicken breasts (or thighs) into a flavorful, crowd-pleasing meal. Plus, it&rsquo;s easy to make ahead, perfect for meal prep, and freezer-friendly, making it ideal for busy weeknights or laid-back weekend BBQs.</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-key-ingredients-for-balsamic-marinade-for-chicken">Key Ingredients for Balsamic Marinade for Chicken</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can find the full list of ingredients for this balsamic vinegar chicken marinade in the recipe card. Below are a few helpful notes to help you make it your own.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-large"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="800" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/chicken-balsamic-marinade-1200x800.jpg" alt="Ingredients for the recipe from the top view." class="wp-image-81783" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/chicken-balsamic-marinade.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/chicken-balsamic-marinade-350x233.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/chicken-balsamic-marinade-768x512.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/chicken-balsamic-marinade-400x267.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/chicken-balsamic-marinade-150x100.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/chicken-balsamic-marinade.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Balsamic vinegar</strong>: When choosing a balsamic vinegar, follow your taste buds and your budget.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">You can use a traditional, aged balsamic from Modena for deeper sweetness and complexity, or a more affordable condiment-grade balsamic vinegar. Both will work beautifully to add that sweet-tangy depth to your chicken.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">I would not recommend substituting store-bought balsamic glaze here, as it is already sweet and thickened. As a result, it won&rsquo;t work the same way in the marinade.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Olive oil</strong>: I recommend using a high-quality extra-virgin olive oil here. Its smooth flavor perfectly balances the tangy balsamic vinegar and creamy Dijon mustard, helping the marinade coat the chicken evenly and soak up all those delicious flavors.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Sweetener: </strong>While I used honey, other liquid sweeteners such as maple syrup and agave can also be used. If you prefer to use brown sugar instead, be sure to stir it thoroughly so that no grainy sugar particles are left behind.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Garlic: </strong>I find that fresh garlic cloves make this recipe shine, but for a milder flavor, you can use &frac12; teaspoon garlic powder (equivalent to 2 cloves of fresh garlic).</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Fresh Herbs: </strong>I think chopped fresh thyme pairs beautifully with the tangy-sweet flavors in this balsamic vinaigrette marinade, but if you don&rsquo;t have fresh thyme, use half the amount of dried thyme instead.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Alternatively, a robust Italian seasoning blend or other fresh (or dried herbs) like rosemary and oregano would also work well in this recipe.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Chicken: </strong>While I used skinless and boneless chicken breasts, you can also use skinless and boneless chicken thighs.&nbsp;</p>



<h2 class="wp-block-heading" id="h-how-to-make-balsamic-chicken-marinade">How To Make Balsamic Chicken Marinade?</h2>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Making this balsamic vinegar marinade for chicken is easy and quick (in fact, the base is very similar to my versatile <a href="https://foolproofliving.com/lemon-balsamic-dressing/">Lemon Balsamic Salad Dressing</a>). Here are the steps:</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/balsamic-vinegar-marinade.jpg" alt="A collage of images showing how to make balsamic marinade for chicken." class="wp-image-81784" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/balsamic-vinegar-marinade.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/balsamic-vinegar-marinade-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/balsamic-vinegar-marinade-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/balsamic-vinegar-marinade-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/balsamic-vinegar-marinade-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/balsamic-vinegar-marinade.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Step 1 &ndash; Mix the Ingredients: </strong>Use a container large enough to comfortably hold two pounds of chicken, ideally one with a tight-fitting lid.&nbsp;</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Place the balsamic vinegar, olive oil, honey, Dijon mustard, minced garlic, thyme, salt, and pepper in the container and whisk until thoroughly combined.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph">Alternatively, you can use a heavy-duty resealable bag, such as a Ziplock bag (for easy cleanup), and pour marinade over the meat. This is especially ideal if you are making it in larger quantities.</p>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Step 2 &ndash; Add the chicken</strong>: Place the chicken in the marinade, making sure each piece is fully coated. Cover tightly with the lid and refrigerate.</p>



<figure class="wp-block-image aligncenter size-full"><img decoding="async" width="1200" height="744" data-pin-nopin="true" src="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/grilled-chicken-marinade-balsamic-vinegar.jpg" alt="Chicken marinating in balsamic marinade from the top view." class="wp-image-81786" srcset="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/grilled-chicken-marinade-balsamic-vinegar.jpg 1200w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/grilled-chicken-marinade-balsamic-vinegar-350x217.jpg 350w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/grilled-chicken-marinade-balsamic-vinegar-768x476.jpg 768w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/grilled-chicken-marinade-balsamic-vinegar-400x248.jpg 400w, https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/grilled-chicken-marinade-balsamic-vinegar-150x93.jpg 150w" sizes="(max-width: 1200px) 100vw, 1200px" data-pin-media="https://foolproofliving.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/06/grilled-chicken-marinade-balsamic-vinegar.jpg"></figure>



<p class="wp-block-paragraph"><strong>Step 3 &ndash; Let time do the rest</strong>: Marinate the chicken in the fridge for at least 30 minutes or, if you have the time, overnight for maximum flavor.</p>
</div>



